The complaint could now be lodged that our newest version of the Functor class is limited
by the fact that it can handle only a member function with prespecified argument and return
types of double and int. This restriction can also be removed using the template approach
(Exercise 8.1). For now, the generality provided by the formulation in Listing 8.5 will be
